    Speed boost, honestly:
      The game rewrites Humanoid.WalkSpeed every frame, so the boost is applied
      as a LinearVelocity constraint instead. Exactly one constraint is ever
      created, it ramps up over ~0.3 s rather than jumping, it only pushes on
      the horizontal axes so gravity and jump height are untouched, it is off
      in water, and it is capped.
      A raw jump to a high velocity is what a server-side movement check reacts
      to; a smooth, capped push in the direction you already walk is the least
      suspicious thing this kind of feature can do.

    Terminology:
      Listener   — the monster (Config.Run.CREATURE.STYLE is literally "Listener")
      Highlight  — a Roblox `Highlight` instance: the through-wall outline
      Billboard  — a `BillboardGui`: the floating label above a part
      Tag        — a Roblox attribute, e.g. `Platform`, `Safe`, `MemTile`, `State`
]]

